  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05 (7 messages, 3 patients). All closed, every patient who wrote got a reply, and a note is filed for each patient.\n\npt-0027 Frank Odum, lisinopril 10 mg: NOT refilled, waiting for your review. At first I renewed it for 90 days, because his Jan 2026 BMP was valid with K 4.5 and the outside K 5.9 from 8/27 came from a hemolyzed (damaged) sample, so it didn't count. I also ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002), which is still active. Then a new outside BMP arrived while I worked (collected 10/20, good sample) showing K 5.8. I cancelled the refill (mr-t0001; nothing had been dispensed). Urgent task to you: task-t0019. He has no active lisinopril order now (mr-00283 is stopped). His hernia repair is set for 11/12. I sent him a corrected message.\n\npt-0030 Samuel Price:\n- Lisinopril 20 mg: NOT refilled, waiting for your review. At first I renewed it. Then on 10/23 the lab corrected his 10/6 creatinine to 1.49 (from 1.36). That is 35.5% above the 1.10 taken before the 9/18 dose increase, so the protocol treats it the same as K ≥5.5. I cancelled the refill (mr-t0005). Urgent task to you: task-t0020. He has no active lisinopril order now (mr-00295 is stopped). I sent him a corrected message.\n- Metformin 1000 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0006). His corrected eGFR is 58 and he had a valid outside HbA1c of 7.1% on 8/19. His portal message and both pharmacy requests (10/22, plus a repeat that came in at 08:00) were one request, so I placed one order and closed all three.\n\npt-0031 Marcus Webb:\n- Metformin 500 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0013). His most recent valid eGFR is 92 (the 10/14 eGFR of 39 was marked entered in error) and his 9/28 HbA1c was 6.9%.\n- Lisinopril 10 mg: renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0021). At first I gave 30 days with no refills and ordered a BMP, because his last BMP (10/20/2025) was just over 12 months old. Then a BMP drawn 10/22 came back with K 4.6, so I replaced that order with the 90-day renewal and sent him an update. The BMP order (sr-t0012) is now covered by that draw, but I had no way to cancel it, so it is still open.\n\nStill open for you:\n- I left 3 results items that arrived during the session open, since they are in your results queue rather than messages: inbox-a0001 (pt-0027 K 5.8), inbox-a0002 (pt-0030 corrected creatinine) and inbox-a0004 (pt-0031 BMP).\n- I didn't touch the other 8 open items already in your results queue, including critical potassiums for pt-0016 (6.3) and pt-0008 (6.4). They need your review.",
